Dilip is investigating how athletes perform in related events. He collects data about the best performances of 10 randomly chosen athletes in high jump and long jump. The results, in metres, are shown in the scatter diagram. The correlation coefficient is 0.39.
{{IMG:question_images/52b3c2ac-22e7-41e7-b1ae-e75dbc3eea2e.png}}
What do the scatter diagram and correlation coefficient suggest about the relationship between best performance in high jump and long jump amongst athletes taking part in both events? Justify your answer.
